What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/local_fault_rate
Date:		May 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write percentage controlling local-fault sampling for
		NUMA memory tiering diagnostics. A value of 0 disables local
		fault sampling. Values from 1 to 100 enable sampling at the
		requested PFN selection rate.

		When non-zero, the local-fault sampler is active even if
		kernel.numa_balancing is 0. In that state regular NUMA balancing
		migration remains disabled, but the local-fault probe/refault
		accounting path can still run.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/local_fault_scan_period_ms
Date:		May 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write scan period, in milliseconds, used by the global
		local-fault sampling scan.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/local_fault_scan_size_mb
Date:		May 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write maximum local-fault scan size, in megabytes, for one
		task NUMA scan period.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/local_fault_refault_hit_ms
Date:		May 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write latency threshold, in milliseconds. Local-fault
		refaults no later than this threshold are counted as hits.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/local_fault_window
Date:		May 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-write sampling window sequence. Reading returns the current
		window sequence. Writing any value advances the window and resets
		the newly selected per-window bucket.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/numa_balancing/local_fault_stats
Date:		May 2026
Contact:	Linux memory management mailing list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Read-only flat-keyed diagnostic file showing global local-fault
		sampling counters, current knob values, and current-window
		PTE/refault/lost-page counters.
